{
  "component": "Switch Field",
  "description": "A labelled on/off switch with an optional description line. Eight variants cover four states (Default, Hover, Focus, Disabled) against two values (Checked, Unchecked), and the label and description can each be switched off.\n\nPURPOSE: Lets a person turn a single setting on or off. The switch sits in a row with its label, and a secondary description can sit below to explain what the setting does.\n\nBEHAVIOUR: The whole field is interactive. Hover gives a lighter brand treatment on the track and border. Focus adds a Stroke/Focus Ring around the control. Disabled swaps text, track, border and knob to the disabled colour set and blocks input. Toggling moves the knob and flips the track between Background/Brand/Default (checked) and Background/Default/Default (unchecked), so the change is immediate with no submit step.\n\nCOMPOSITION: No nested component instances were detected. Each variant is built from a \"Checkbox and Label\" frame holding a Label text layer and a \"Switch\" frame with one child knob layer, plus a Description text layer below. Before building this, AI code generators should check the development codebase for an existing Switch or Toggle primitive and a form field wrapper, and reuse them rather than rebuilding the track and knob.\n\nUSAGE: Use for settings that apply straight away, such as notifications or visibility. Use a Checkbox Field instead when the choice is part of a form that gets submitted, or when several options can be picked from a list. Use radio buttons for mutually exclusive choices. Turn off Has Description when the label is self-explanatory, and turn off Has Label only when an adjacent element already names the setting.\n\nCODE GENERATION NOTES: Render as input type=checkbox with role=\"switch\", or the platform switch control, not a styled div. Tie the Label to the input with a for/id pair and point aria-describedby at the Description so screen readers read both. Hover and Focus are CSS states, not props, so do not expose them as an API; only Disabled and the checked value should be real props. Focus must be reachable by keyboard and toggle with Space. The Disabled variant should set the disabled attribute rather than only changing colour. Keep the track pill shape with Radius/Full and the row gap with Space/300.",
